.TH WMGFX 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmgfx \- detect the graphics hardware and print an X11 tearing fix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmgfx
detect | xorg | picom | apply [\-\-system] | autostart
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdetect\fR reads /sys/class/drm and names the GPU driver. \fBxorg\fR and \fBpicom\fR print a configuration suited to it
(an Xorg TearFree snippet, or a picom configuration); \fBautostart\fR prints the picom command line.
\fBapply\fR writes the picom configuration to ~/.config/picom/picom.conf; with \fB\-\-system\fR it also writes the
Xorg driver snippet to /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/20\-wm\-desktop\-gpu.conf (needs root).
